      sources: "Sources: Learn, app management policies API overview; removePassword; workload identities; appliedConditionalAccessPolicy (beta); gMSAs. Chapter 11, Step 1.6.",
      say: `The smoke test proves the deployment end to end on objects nobody depends on, and you write each expected result down before it runs. The synthetic app must appear in the register with two owners and no secret. The synthetic service account must be rated high. A new secret on the synthetic app must be refused, and if it isn't, it's removed at once. The federated credential must match exactly. Each workload policy must be report-only, with the synthetic assigned directly. The sign-ins must show the report-only results, from a beta read. And the test host must retrieve the group managed account's password.`,
      detail: `Step 1.6 expected results (not yet observed live). ST-01, G1: the synthetic app in the register with OwnerCount 2, Secrets 0, CredentialKind Federated (the inventory and the ownership rule see a new app). ST-02, G1: svc-npi-smoke rated HIGH, password never expires (the inventory flags what the guide's first wave converts). ST-03, G3: the new secret refused; the pilot policy blocks password addition on the synthetic app; if it is accepted, the script removes it by key ID at once and the check fails; a 401 or 403 also fails, as a permission problem, not the policy. ST-04, G5: one federated credential matching issuer, subject and the single audience exactly (Chapter 05's exact, case-sensitive match). ST-05, G4: each workload policy enabledForReportingButNotEnforced, the synthetic's object ID in includeServicePrincipals (direct assignment, report-only). ST-06, G4: the synthetic's sign-ins show reportOnlyFailure for CA015 from the outside run and reportOnlyNotApplied from the inside run; report-only results are returned only with the Prefer: include-unknown-enum-members header (Graph beta). ST-07, G5: Test-ADServiceAccount True and the synthetic account enabled; the host can retrieve the gMSA's password. The last line is Result: PASS, or Result: FAIL. Stop here and run the rollback., with exit code 1. Evidence: SMOKE-smoke-test.json supports AC-2, CM-8, IA-4 and OMB M-22-09 §III.A (ST-01, ST-02); IA-5 and SCuBA MS.AAD.5.5v1, SHOULD (ST-03); IA-5, IA-9 (ST-04, ST-07); AC-3, AC-6, IA-9 (ST-05); AU-2, AU-12, CA-7 (ST-06).`,
