      say: `Now the dry run, the chapter's own commands on the kit's fixtures, run on November twenty-first in a scratch copy of the kit. Nothing leaves the machine. The test preflight prints twelve passes and one warning. The settings file is clean, the deployment identity uses a certificate, the Workload ID Premium license is there, the baseline is recorded, and the test host and its group exist. The warning is deliberate: the fixture's Conditional Access administrator holds a standing role, not one eligible through PIM. Then the group managed account plan: one outbound-only account, run by the pipeline, with its SailPoint request and change record.`,
      detail: `Dry run on the kit's fixtures, run November 21, 2026 (Windows 11, PowerShell 7.6) in a scratch copy of examples/non-person-identity, with the chapter's commands; the output matches the chapter's dry run line for line, including every hash. Commands: Set-Location <kit-folder>; ./deploy/Test-NpiDeployPreflight.ps1 -SettingsPath tests/fixtures/deploy/settings.test.json -Stage test -BaselinePath tests/fixtures/deploy/vk-baseline.json -FixturePath tests/fixtures/deploy/tenant-test.json -OutputPath out/dryrun/test-preflight; ./deploy/New-NpiDeploySmokeGmsaPlan.ps1 -SettingsPath tests/fixtures/deploy/settings.test.json -Stage test -OutputPath out/dryrun/test-gmsa-plan -AsOf '2026-11-02T12:00:00Z'. Full preflight: PF-01 Pass (settings file, test, gcc, sha256 bea7ef8879f0); PF-02 Pass (0 secrets, 1 certificate); PF-03 Pass (Workload_Identities_P2, 5 enabled units); PF-04 Pass (Entra ID P1 or P2 for the service principal sign-in logs: SPE_E5); PF-05 Pass (reader holds Graph read permissions only); PF-06 Pass (identity engineer: Cloud Application Administrator eligible; Security Administrator eligible); PF-06 Warn (Conditional Access administrator: Conditional Access Administrator active); PF-07 Pass (pilot Payroll Export, AzureADMyOrg, 1 secret; synthetic npi-smoke-test, 0 secrets); PF-08 Pass (CA015-ServiceAccounts-LocationRestriction-Ring1 and CA037-WorkloadIdentities-HighRisk-Block-Ring1 enabledForReportingButNotEnforced); PF-09 Pass (VK-NPI baseline: 01 Fail 4; 02 Fail 2; 03 Fail 1; 04 Fail 3; 05 Warn 3; 06 Fail 2; 07 Warn 1; 08 Fail 1); PF-10 Pass (app-test-01.corp-test.contoso.example; DL-gMSA-npismoke-Hosts). The gMSA plan: CreateGmsa gmsa-npismoke$ in OU=Service Accounts,DC=corp-test,DC=contoso,DC=example, retriever CN=DL-gMSA-npismoke-Hosts,OU=Groups,DC=corp-test,DC=contoso,DC=example; runBy pipeline; request SP-REQ-0002001, change CHG-2026-1102-T; outbound-only because the smoke test's service needs no SPN (WD-154). The test preflight's one Warn is deliberate: the fixture's Conditional Access administrator holds a standing assignment instead of a PIM-eligible one, which the preflight reports but doesn't block (design guidance). Learn: Workload ID Premium is needed to create or change a policy scoped to service principals (PF-03); PF-06 reads PIM-eligible roles from roleEligibilityScheduleInstances.`,
