      say: `Stage 1 starts by preparing: the group managed account's retriever group with the test host in it, and the synthetic objects, an app with two owners and a federated credential, and a service account whose random password nobody records. The pilot's policy is created, turned off. The preflight records the validation kit's baseline, checks one to ten; check ten, for AWS GovCloud and O C I, doesn't apply in this Entra runbook. And it checks the root key is more than ten hours old. Step 1.1 reads every identity and its owners. Step 1.2 turns the pilot policy on for just two apps, and plans the tenant-wide one for review. Step 1.3 moves the pilot to a federated credential and a managed identity, beside its old secret.`,
      detail: `Prepare (once per stage, after the change record is approved, before the preflight): create the inputs folders with header rows only where a file doesn't exist; the forest's ad-standard.json from Chapter 06's fixture with the stage forest's OUs (expected: the two OUs, DL-gMSA-Creators and 30), reviewed by AD engineering with its SHA-256 in the change record; New-ADGroup DL-gMSA-<app>-Hosts -GroupScope DomainLocal and Add-ADGroupMember the test host (Learn suggests a security group of the hosts allowed to retrieve a gMSA's password; PF-10 fails if it isn't domain local; restart the host before Step 1.4); the synthetic app registration and service principal (npi-smoke-<stage>, AzureADMyOrg, two owners who are the operators, a federated credential repo:<repository>:environment:<stage>, audience api://AzureADTokenExchange, no secret); the synthetic service account with New-ADUser -AccountPassword (48 random bytes) -Enabled -PasswordNeverExpires, so the register must rate it HIGH; the pilot's app management policy, isEnabled false, blocking passwordAddition and symmetricKeyAddition and capping asymmetricKeyLifetime at P180D, restrictForAppsCreatedAfterDateTime 2015-01-01; re-read the settings file (three GUIDs). Preflight: ../validation-kit/Invoke-ValidationKit.ps1 -Track NPI -IncludePreview -SkipConnect (VK-NPI-01 to VK-NPI-10; VK-NPI-10, the AWS GovCloud (US) and OCI check, is NotApplicable here, because it reads the implementation guide's Step 1g and 1h exports, which this Entra runbook doesn't make; a Fail is a baseline, an Error a blocker; VK-NPI-09 reads a beta API); Test-NpiDeployPreflight.ps1 (in Stage 2 with -PromotionEvidencePath); the KDS root key's msKds-UseStartTime more than 10 hours ago, read with Chapter 06's delegated read, not Get-KdsRootKey; if none, Add-KdsRootKey -EffectiveImmediately and wait 10 hours; Learn's backdated key is for a test environment with one domain controller only. Step 1.1 (G1): Invoke-NpiInventory.ps1 and Invoke-NpiOwnership.ps1 as the reader app; expected: the synthetic app with OwnerCount 2, Secrets 0, CredentialKind Federated, the pilot with its one secret, svc-npi-smoke Risk HIGH; SQL Server's principals in data-platform-handoff.csv; the orphan plan isn't applied. Evidence S1.1 supports AC-2, CM-8, IA-4 and OMB M-22-09 §III.A. Step 1.2 (G3): PATCH the pilot policy isEnabled true and assign it to the pilot and synthetic apps through appManagementPolicies/$ref, or in the admin center (Entra ID > Enterprise apps > Application policies > Block password addition > Select applications), one or the other, since an application holds only one custom policy; Learn documents no report-only mode, so the scope is the safety; then Invoke-NpiCredentialPolicy.ps1 plans the tenant-wide policy and its hash goes to the reviewer for Stage 2. Evidence S1.2 supports IA-5, CM-3, CM-6 and SCuBA MS.AAD.5.5v1 to 5.7v1 (SHOULD). Step 1.3 (G5): az identity create as the identity engineer; write the conversion file (pilot-01 the GitHub workflow's secret to a federated credential; pilot-02 the legacy AD account to a user-assigned managed identity); Invoke-NpiFederation.ps1 plan, hash, dry run and -Apply; a wrong subject fails only at the exchange; AADSTS70021 may appear while the credential propagates; the owner records the cutover; the old secret stays until the owner removes it in a separate reviewed change. Evidence S1.3 supports IA-5, IA-9, CM-3(2), CM-4(2) and AC-2(3).`,
