      sources: "Sources: Chapter 11, “Promotion go/no-go criteria.”",
      say: `Production starts only when nine criteria are signed. The test smoke test passed every check, after the rollback and re-deployment. The rollback was rehearsed and filed. Every hash in the evidence folder matches. Fourteen days of report-only sign-ins were reviewed, with no unexpected failure from inside the egress range. The tenant-wide policy plan was approved. Production's settings, licenses and PIM eligibility are in place. The change record is approved. And the evidence check passes.`,
      detail: `Production starts only when every row is signed (design guidance). Evidence per row: 1, smoke-final/results.json, all Pass (identity engineer); 2, rollback-apply/results.json, all Applied or AlreadyDone, and the after-rollback preflight (Conditional Access administrator); 3, sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS output (ISSO); 4, Chapter 08's signin-summary.json and its SHA-256 (Conditional Access administrator); 5, policy-plan/policy-plan.json and the approval (identity governance officer); 6, the production settings file's SHA-256 (identity governance officer); 7, a production preflight run before the window with no Fail (identity engineer); 8, the change record (change advisory board); 9, Test-NpiDeployEvidence.ps1 for the test stage, exit 0: Result: every requirement row has its evidence, and every hash matches. (ISSO). Row 9 expects one Present row for each of PRE, S0, S1.1, S1.2, S1.3, S1.5, SMOKE, ROLLBACK and EVIDENCE; any Missing, Failing or WrongEnvironment row is a no-go. Rows 1 and 2 in one command: 8 Pass for the smoke test, 5 Applied (or some AlreadyDone) for the rollback. The 14-day summary for row 4: Invoke-NpiWorkloadCa.ps1 -Mode SignIns as the reader app (AuditLog.Read.All and Policy.Read.ConditionalAccess).`,
      cite: [],
      ref: "“Promotion go/no-go criteria”",
